BACKPORT: 5 bug fixes for the emergent-v3 (EC2 + Cloudflare prod) branch
=========================================================================
Verified with `git apply --check` against origin/emergent-v3 @ e3e48df0
(2026-07-20). Contains ONLY the 5 fixes — no migration-specific changes
(no PUBLIC_APP_URL de-hardcoding, no env/URL changes).

  1. backend/routes/acm.py             — NEW GET /api/acm/health (admin-gated;
                                         returns status/seeded/modules/features_loaded;
                                         stops the admin-dashboard 404 poll)
  2. backend/routes/ai_tools.py        — input validation on POST /api/ai/prioritize-factors
                                         (malformed body -> 400/422 instead of 500;
                                         valid requests unchanged)
  3. backend/routes/report_shares.py   — ShareCreate.module/channel as Literal enums
                                         (documented in OpenAPI; invalid module -> 422
                                         listing valid values)
  4. frontend/app/share/invite/[id].tsx — logged-out redirect /login -> /auth/login
                                         (was an unmatched Expo Router route)
  5. frontend/app/tools/pros-cons.tsx  — declarative <Redirect> instead of
                                         router.replace-in-useEffect: direct deep-links
                                         could crash with "Attempted to navigate before
                                         mounting the Root Layout component" and hang on
                                         the "Updating to the latest version..." splash

HOW TO APPLY (on your machine / EC2 checkout):
  git checkout emergent-v3
  git pull origin emergent-v3
  git apply --check backport_5fixes_for_emergent-v3.patch   # dry-run, must be silent
  git apply backport_5fixes_for_emergent-v3.patch
  git commit -am "fix: acm/health endpoint, prioritize-factors validation, shares module enum, share-invite login redirect, pros-cons deep-link crash (backport)"
  git push origin emergent-v3

THEN DEPLOY VIA YOUR NORMAL FLOW:
  - Backend:  ssh EC2 && cd /opt/dezider && ./deploy/sync.sh     (fixes 1-3)
  - Frontend: push to emergent-v3 triggers Cloudflare Pages auto-build (fixes 4-5)
  (Both needed — see DEPLOY.md two-pipeline note.)

